 cuda-cudart-12-9,
 libcublas-12-9,
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: llama-cpp-python dynamic CUDA 12.9 backend
 This package contains the dynamically loadable CUDA backend for
 llama-cpp-python, built with the NVIDIA CUDA 12.9 toolkit.
 Multiple versioned CUDA backend packages may be installed in parallel;
 update-alternatives selects the default CUDA backend.

Package: python3-llama-cpp-python-backend-cuda13.3
Architecture: any
Provides: python3-llama-cpp-python-backend-cuda (= ${binary:Version})
Depends:
 python3-llama-cpp-python (= ${binary:Version}),
 cuda-cudart-13-3,
 libcublas-13-3,
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: llama-cpp-python dynamic CUDA 13.3 backend
 This package contains the dynamically loadable CUDA backend for
 llama-cpp-python, built with the NVIDIA CUDA 13.3 toolkit.
 Multiple versioned CUDA backend packages may be installed in parallel;
 update-alternatives selects the default CUDA backend.

Package: python3-llama-cpp-python-backend-rocm7.14
Architecture: amd64
Provides: python3-llama-cpp-python-backend-rocm (= ${binary:Version})
Depends:
 python3-llama-cpp-python (= ${binary:Version}),
 amdrocm-runtime7.14,
 amdrocm-blas7.14,
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: llama-cpp-python dynamic ROCm 7.14 HIP backend
 This package contains the dynamically loadable HIP backend for
 llama-cpp-python, built with AMD ROCm Core SDK 7.14.  It contains code
 objects for a broad set of GCN, RDNA and CDNA targets.  Unsupported Vega
 APUs may also be usable with HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION where compatible.
 Multiple versioned ROCm backend packages may be installed in parallel;
 update-alternatives selects the default ROCm backend.

Package: python3-llama-cpp-python-backend-sycl
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 python3-llama-cpp-python (= ${binary:Version}),
 intel-oneapi-compiler-dpcpp-cpp-runtime,
 intel-oneapi-mkl-sycl-blas,
 intel-oneapi-dnnl,
 intel-oneapi-tbb,
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: llama-cpp-python dynamic Intel SYCL backend
 This package contains the dynamically loadable SYCL backend for
 llama-cpp-python, built with Intel oneAPI DPC++/C++.  It targets Intel
 GPUs through SYCL/Level Zero, uses FP16 kernels, oneMKL SYCL BLAS and
 oneDNN, and keeps the backend separate from the common Python runtime.

Package: python3-llama-cpp
Architecture: any
Section: oldlibs
Depends:
